DISPOSITION
================================================================================
A complete, HIG-native SwiftUI FeatureFlagsPage shipped at parity with the web source: a pure
@Observable state holder (ADR-004 — no networking in the view) exposing per-source
loading/empty/success/error over an injectable feature-flag repository seam (default = an
in-memory registry seeded with representative flags + an audit feed, matching the manifest's
"renders from local state"); two titled glass panels (Registry + Recent changes) built from the
shared P2 tokens + P3 components (TSGlassPanel/TSDataTable/TSEmptyState/TSErrorDisplay/
TSTableSkeleton/TSButton/TSTextField/TSTextArea/typography) and the canonical feature-flag domain
types (FeatureFlagEntry/FeatureFlagChange/FlagValue/ChangeJSONValue) shared with the FlagsTable/
ChangesPanel components — no duplicated domain model; an adaptive header (macOS/iPad row vs iPhone
compact stack) with an Add CTA; a trailing create/edit drawer (useSetFlag) with live JSON
validation; and a reason-gated delete Modal (useDeleteFlag). Every visible string resolves from
Localizable.xcstrings with web key names; full VoiceOver labels/traits on both panels, rows, the
operation chip, and the editor; deep-linkable via the new .featureFlags route (AppRouteParser maps
both /feature-flags and the web /admin/flags) and hosted through the shell's route registry.
Verified on BOTH idioms by isolated Swift 6 strict-concurrency type-checks (0/0) and an executed
model harness (22/22). The full xcodebuild scheme is RED ONLY due to 73 pre-existing, out-of-scope
sibling escaping-closure bugs + a toolchain IR crash (forbidden to commit-fix), with ZERO
diagnostics in any of my files (proven by a temporary-fix-then-revert pass).

